# Concept 3 — Hero + Satellites (one purpose per dashboard)

Philosophy: every dashboard answers ONE question. A single hero widget
dominates (~2/3 canvas); satellites give context around it. Encourages
many small dashboards over one mega-dashboard — pairs with sidebar
sections as the navigation between them.

```
+------------------------------------------+-----------+
| HERO: TASKS (assignee: me)               | METRIC    |
|                                          | open: 12  |
|  [ All | Mine | Unassigned ]   (+ task)  +-----------+
|                                          | METRIC    |
|  TODO                                    | overdue: 3|
|   [ ] Ship sidebar sections      jun 13  +-----------+
|   [ ] Restart dev API            jun 12  | TREND 7d  |
|   [ ] Review vendor sheet        jun 14  |    .x     |
|  IN PROGRESS                             |  x.x x.x  |
|   [~] Dashboard redesign         jun 12  | --------- |
|   [~] 0022 migration cleanup     jun 13  +-----------+
|  DONE (3)                       (show)   | ACTIVITY  |
|                                          | 10:42 anna|
|                                          | 10:31 jens|
|                                          | 09:58 mia |
+------------------------------------------+-----------+
```

Composition rule: exactly one hero (list / tasks / kanban / calendar),
satellites limited to small kinds (metric / trend / attention /
activity). Editor could enforce: "pick hero, then add satellites".

Best for: personal home, per-concept default dashboards ("the Vendors
dashboard" = hero list of vendors + vendor stats).
Risk: weak fit for genuine multi-topic overviews.
